Beat files for the lead recording, one per cohort session, named after the
session. demo/stub-claude plays the file matching its own -n name, so a session
with no file here just idles at a prompt.

Fields are tab separated: <kind><TAB><text><TAB><extra>

  say      The person at the keyboard types <text> and sends it.
  reply    Claude answers with <text>. <extra> overrides the pause after it.
  tool     Claude runs something. <text> is what the tool call shows; <extra>,
           when given, is what actually runs instead. The output under it is
           the real command's real output.
  pause    Sleep <text> seconds.
  attach   Block until somebody is looking at this session. Everything after it
           plays to an audience, and since there is only ever one client, this
           is what keeps two sessions' scripts from talking over each other.
  switch   Open the tmux session picker and choose <text>, the way the prefix
           key would. <extra> overrides the pause before it.
  detach   Hand the terminal back to the shell the recording started from.

Lines starting with # are ignored.
